  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 14-layer dielectric stack on fused silica substrate for solar-blind UV filtering. Materials: HfO2 (high-index), Al2O3 (medium-index), SiO2 (low-index). Layer sequence from air: HfO2, Al2O3, SiO2, HfO2, Al2O3, SiO2, HfO2, HfO2, SiO2, Al2O3, SiO2, HfO2, Al2O3, SiO2. Initialize high-index layers at 15-20nm QWOT for 267nm center wavelength. Initialize low-index SiO2 spacers at quarter-wave optical thickness for 267nm. Optimize all 14 thicknesses using gradient-based optimizer with bounds 10-150nm. Evaluate transmittance at normal incidence across 255-280nm (passband), 300-700nm (visible stopband), and 700-1100nm (NIR stopband). Score candidates by mean passband transmittance minus mean stopband transmittance. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 255–280 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Transmittance in 300–700 nm; Transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers; No metal layers; Only conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize all 14 thicknesses of a dielectric stack (HfO2/Al2O3/SiO2 sequence) on fused silica for normal incidence. Maximize mean transmittance in 255-280 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm. Optimizer bounds: 10-150 nm per layer.",
